# MEASURED 2026-09-21: hypothesis writes `.hypothesis/.gitignore` containing `*`, so the
# directory hid itself and was ignored by nothing this tree says. The pre-tag receipt gate
# counts an ignore file that only a non-tracked source accounts for as dirt (that is the
# shape of a planted `sub/.gitignore` beside a planted `sub/evil.py`), and the audit it
# runs uses hypothesis in ten test modules. The tree names the cache itself.
.hypothesis/
.coverage
htmlcov/

